Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:11:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Exercise runtime block preview ownership and recovery fences

Use the existing accepted fork fixtures to compare runtime preview with direct local construction and prove that preview preserves epochs, parent state and staged selection. Check typed stale/capacity/pending outcomes, callback Busy access and moved-from Closed access without publishing caller outputs.

The combined signed assembler and facade suites pass Debug and Release against preview core 7c8ced2fc, assembler 2350e1544 and runtime facade b968c50a8. This is test-only evidence; borrowed production sources and build outputs are excluded, and preview success makes no acceptance or time-eligibility claim.
---
